Chapter: ChapterPaginationUnmarked

 Two chapters share a name and neither numbers its pages. That is
 indistinguishable from an ACCIDENTAL duplicate: the definitions merge
 under one slug, a name defined in both collides or shadows, and before
 CDX3004 this compiled clean and ran, printing 3.

 A chapter that spans files must say so. That is what tells a deliberate
 page apart from a collision.

Section: First
  alpha : Integer
  alpha = 1

Chapter: ChapterPaginationUnmarked

Section: Second
  beta : Integer
  beta = 2

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (show (alpha + beta))
  end
